# OS
.DS_Store

# Go
/bin/
/dist/
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# The local build of the checker. `go build -o agent-conform ./cmd/agent-conform`
# is the obvious thing to type, and it lands at the root, which /bin/ and /dist/
# do not cover. It has to be ignored rather than merely untracked: Go stamps
# vcs.modified into the binary, ONE untracked file in the checkout flips it to
# true, and that changes the bytes of every later build. The reproducibility
# recipe in the README depends on `git status --porcelain` printing nothing.
/agent-conform

# Editor
.idea/
.vscode/

# Session / tooling (not part of the project)
.remember/
.claude/
